      "id": 1,
      "text": "Olivet was founded in 1844 and quickly became a college town, with Olivet College standing out for its early commitment to coeducation and inclusion.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://thumbwind.com/2026/04/16/history-of-olivet-michigan/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The arrival of the Grand Trunk Railroad gave Olivet its first major advantage, turning the town into a rail hub for farmers and merchants.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://thumbwind.com/2026/04/16/history-of-olivet-michigan/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Olivet’s history shows a community that balanced work and social life in a compact, walkable area, keeping the town small and close‑knit.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://thumbwind.com/2026/04/16/history-of-olivet-michigan/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Olivet College remains a cultural anchor, with its library and campus events drawing visitors and shaping the town’s identity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://thumbwind.com/2026/04/16/history-of-olivet-michigan/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
